From 1cf650360ed874cb10d27ca0877207c2b272a797 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:32:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve review custody across admission retry parks

Review admission exhaustion was recorded as gave_up. Timed scheduling then
forgot the review phase, so a wake escalated to a deep implementer and its
no-code re-handoff consumed another independent reviewer.

Preserve the resumable phase in schedule/unblock, exclude typed admission
refusals (and narrow legacy equivalents) from implementation escalation,
and retain original author custody for repeated immutable merged PR/head/
merge identities. Unknown/changed artifacts and intervening executed work
remain author evidence; no blanket review_requested exemption.

Proof:
- Regression RED reproduced author pollution, phase loss, and deep retry.
- 578 tests passed, 1 skipped across 28 review/tier/park/wake consumer files.
- 13/13 distinct mutants killed; two initial survivors gained repeated-
  invalid-identity controls and were killed on rerun.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks pass.
- Read-only replay over 20 hub board/shadow DBs, deduped by task/run UID:
  only the example card's model re-handoffs are exempted; 25 review-admission
  gave_up receipts stop counting as implementation failures. Inspected
  every changed input; no implementation failure was exempted.

Hotspots: kanban_review_model.py overlaps review-author-custody; kanban_db.py
changes only two existing lines for scheduled phase readback/unblock.
